            <ArticleTitle>Effect of glyceryl guaiacolate in animal models of inflammation and pain.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>285-93</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A weak but significant anti-inflammatory and analgesic effect has been shown for glyceryl guaiacolate (GG) in the laboratory rat. Its potency was less than that observed for acetylsalicylic acid (ASA).</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
